--- a/Telegram/SourceFiles/AGENTS.md
+++ b/Telegram/SourceFiles/AGENTS.md
@@ -386,6 +386,12 @@ This atlas divides Telegram Desktop's sources into named areas, ordered from fou
 - Paths: `SourceFiles/platform/`, `SourceFiles/webauthn/`, `SourceFiles/data/data_passkey_deserialize*`, `SourceFiles/menu/menu_dock*`, `SourceFiles/_other/startup_task_win.cpp`
 - Linux, macOS and Windows implementations behind `platform_*.h`: native window and title, notification backends, tray, launcher and autostart, file dialogs, overlay helpers, OCR, translation providers, wallet key protection, passkeys with caBLE and FIDO2, the Touch Bar and the Dock menu. It must not hold cross-platform feature logic. Today it also holds the shared caBLE passkey protocol, ceremony and QR box in `webauthn/`, which every OS backend calls; that belongs in a passkeys feature area, which does not exist yet.
 
+## Lumengram
+
+### lumen — Lumengram additions
+- Paths: `SourceFiles/lumen/`
+- Lumengram-only features kept apart from upstream areas so upstream merges stay small: the animated login background with the next button pulse, the login entrance and the step crossfade, the Lumengram settings section, the ghost mode switches with their stored values and their main menu and tray toggles, the offline and read requests ghost mode sends after a message, branding names, Lumen themes, peer ID and DC lines, streamer mode, appearance switches, liquid glass bars, the in-memory saved deleted messages and edit history, and the developer and supporter badges. Upstream areas only hold the hooks that call into it, for ghost mode a `Lumen::GhostActive` check before a request. It must not change network behavior unless the user turned on an option for that.
+
